{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 Phoenix\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Analog Tape Saturator with 5 selectable tape saturation topologies and 3 high-frequency flux responses.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 Features\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab 5 selectable tape saturation topologies: Luminescent, Iridescent, Radiant, Luster, and Dark Essence\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab 3 high-frequency flux responses: Opal (Neutral), Gold (Warm), and Sapphire (Bright)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Input trim, process, and output trim controls\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Auto-gain compensation mode\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Calibrated studio peak and RMS metering with clip indicators\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Scalable HiDPI text zoom\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 Credits\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Core DSP algorithms by JClones (https://github.com/JClones/JSFXClones), licensed under MIT.\sa180\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 MemoryAPI JSFX Repository\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A collection of custom audio DSP effects and JSFX plugins for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reaper.fm/"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Cockos REAPER
}}}
, packaged for seamless installation and automatic updates via {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reapack.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
ReaPack
}}}
.\par}
{\pard \qc \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \emdash\emdash\emdash\emdash\emdash\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 \u55357 ?\u56550 ? How to Install via ReaPack\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab Ensure {\b ReaPack} is installed in REAPER (included by default in many setups, or downloadable from {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://reapack.com"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
reapack.com
}}}
).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab In REAPER's top menu, go to: {\b Extensions} > {\b ReaPack} > {\b Import repositories...}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 3.\tx360\tab Paste your repository URL:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi0 \f1 https://raw.githubusercontent.com/memoryapi/memoryapi-jsfx/master/index.xml\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 4.\tx360\tab Click {\b OK}. ReaPack will fetch the repository index.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 5.\tx360\tab In REAPER, go to: {\b Extensions} > {\b ReaPack} > {\b Browse packages...}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 6.\tx360\tab Search for {\f1 SpectralCarver} (or any plugin from this repo), right-click the package, select {\b Install}, and click {\b Apply}.\sa180\par}
{\pard \qc \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \emdash\emdash\emdash\emdash\emdash\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 \u55356 ?\u57243 ? Included Plugins\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 1. Dynamics / SpectralCarver\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Path}: {\f1 Dynamics/SpectralCarver.jsfx}\line {\b Description}: 32-Band Dynamic Spectral Ducker with Cytomic State Variable Filters (SVF)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\cf1 [image: screenshots/spectralcarver.webp]\cf0}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Key Features}:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b 32-Band SVF Dynamic Carving}: Frequency-dependent ducking that attenuates only the frequencies active in the sidechain, keeping the mix clean and preserving headroom without traditional broadband pumping.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Routing}: Route your kick, vocals, or sidechain trigger audio to {\b Channels 3/4} of the track.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Interactive Spectrum Display}: Visual real-time sidechain energy and gain reduction meters with draggable Low-Cut and High-Cut filter boundary curtains.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Redesigned Animated UI}: Modern design with hover halos, animated collapsible drawer, and selectable UI Text Zoom (100%/120%/140%) for HiDPI displays.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Stereo & Mid/Side Processing}: Switchable between L/R stereo ducking and M/S ducking (with dedicated M/S width balance).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Freeze & Audition}: Freeze the current sidechain profile into a static carving EQ curve, or audition the filtered sidechain signal.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Safe DSP Ceiling}: Hard NaN/Inf protection and anti-explosion audio ceilings.\sa180\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 2. Dynamics / Opto2A\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Path}: {\f1 Dynamics/Opto2A.jsfx}\line {\b Description}: Optical Tube Compressor\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\cf1 [image: screenshots/opto2a.webp]\cf0}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Key Features}:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b T4 Optical Attenuator Modeling}: Smooth, program-dependent compression curve with characteristic two-stage multi-exponential release memory.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Compress / Limit Modes}: Switchable knee characteristics from gentle musical leveling to peak limiting.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b HF Emphasis (R37)}: Dedicated sidechain high-pass emphasis control for frequency-conscious vocal leveling and de-essing.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Classic vs. Fast Photocell Speed}: Switch between vintage relaxed optical response and modern fast response.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Dual Display Metering}: Illuminated vintage VU meter with real-time scrolling Gain Reduction trace graph.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b HiDPI Text Scaling}: Quick toggle for 100%, 120%, and 140% UI text zoom.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Credits}: DSP algorithms by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/JClones/JSFXClones"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
JClones
}}}
, licensed under MIT.\sa180\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 3. Dynamics / OverTop\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Path}: {\f1 Dynamics/OverTop.jsfx}\line {\b Description}: 3-Band Upward/Downward Multiband Compressor (OTT Style)\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\cf1 [image: screenshots/overtop.webp]\cf0}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Key Features}:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b 3-Band Upward & Downward Dynamics}: Multiband processing with independent upward compression (lifting quiet details) and downward compression (controlling aggressive peaks).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Interactive Threshold Bars}: Drag horizontally on any band's level bar to offset thresholds with instantaneous visual feedback.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Per-Band Gain & Bypass}: Dedicated bypass toggle and +/-24 dB output gain control for Low (<88 Hz), Mid, and High (>2.5 kHz) bands.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Global Controls}: Depth percentage (dry/wet scaling), Time scaling (1% to 1000%), and Master Input/Output gain trims.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Dedicated Upward % & Downward %}: Balance upward vs downward compression intensity from 0% to 200%.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Modern Vector UI}: Real-time level meters, gain reduction indicators, and scalable HiDPI text zoom (100% - 140%).\sa180\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 4. Dynamics / PulseDuck\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Path}: {\f1 Dynamics/PulseDuck.jsfx}\line {\b Description}: Multiband Sidechain & Envelope Shaper\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\cf1 [image: screenshots/pulseduck.webp]\cf0}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Key Features}:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b 16 Instant Curve Presets}: Classic, tight, offbeat, tremolo, and trance gate ducking shapes, plus custom breakpoint node editing with tension curves.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b 4 Trigger Modes}: Tempo Sync (Repeat), MIDI Note, External Sidechain (Ch 3/4), and Audio Input.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Multiband Crossover}: Full-band, 2-band (Lo/Hi), and 3-band (Lo/Mid/Hi) ducking with 12/24 dB slopes and Band Solo.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Dual Real-Time Scope}: Overlay ducked bass audio (white) directly over incoming sidechain trigger kick (yellow).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b One-Click Trace SC}: Automatically detects and fits the ducking curve around your incoming kick transient.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Groove Shaping}: Variable curve slope, timing offset, and phase shift controls (<< < > >>) to lock the pocket.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Scalable UI}: HiDPI text zoom presets (100% - 140%).\sa180\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 5. Saturation / OInflator\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Path}: {\f1 Saturation/OInflator.jsfx}\line {\b Description}: Harmonic Waveshaper & Loudness Enhancer\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\cf1 [image: screenshots/oinflator.webp]\cf0}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Key Features}:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Authentic Transfer Curve Waveshaping}: Specialized polynomial waveshaping algorithm that increases perceived loudness, warmth, and density without destroying transient punch.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Real-time Harmonic Transfer Viewport}: Live visual representation of the transfer curve and operating point with instantaneous boost dB readout.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Phase-Compensated Band Split}: Switchable 3-band split mode with 240 Hz and 2.4 kHz crossovers for independent multiband harmonic excitement.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Clip 0dB Protection}: Prevents signals from exceeding 0 dBFS ceiling when active.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Calibrated Studio Metering}: High-resolution input/output peak and RMS bar meters with hold decay and clip latches.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b HiDPI Text Scaling}: Quick toggle for 100%, 120%, and 140% UI text zoom.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Credits}: DSP algorithms by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/JClones/JSFXClones"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
JClones
}}}
, licensed under MIT.\sa180\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 6. Saturation / Phoenix\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Path}: {\f1 Saturation/Phoenix.jsfx}\line {\b Description}: Analog Tape Saturator\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\cf1 [image: screenshots/phoenix.webp]\cf0}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Key Features}:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b 5 Tape Topologies}: Selectable analog saturation types (Luminescent, Iridescent, Radiant, Luster, and Dark Essence).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b 3 Brightness Curves}: Switchable high-frequency tape flux responses (Opal for neutral, Gold for warm, Sapphire for bright).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Input & Output Trims with Auto-Gain}: Input Trim (-10 to +10 dB), Process amount (0 to 100%), Output Trim (-6 to +6 dB), and optional automatic gain compensation.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Studio Metering & HiDPI Zoom}: Dual input/output peak/RMS meters with OVER clip indicators and selectable UI text scaling.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Credits}: DSP algorithms by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://github.com/JClones/JSFXClones"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
JClones
}}}
, licensed under MIT.\sa180\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 7. Creative / ChronoWarp\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Path}: {\f1 Creative/ChronoWarp.jsfx}\line {\b Description}: Creative Half-Time & Varispeed Engine\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\cf1 [image: screenshots/chronowarp.webp]\cf0}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Key Features}:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b 3 Speed Modes}: 1.5x (-5 semitones triplet), 2x Half-Time (-1 octave half-speed), and 4x Quarter-Time (-2 octaves quad-slow).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Continuous Ring-Buffer DSP}: 4-point Hermite cubic interpolation over an ~87-second continuous ring buffer for artifact-free, clickless time transformation.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Synchronized Loop Lengths}: Quantized to project tempo from 1/16 beat up to 8 full bars.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Bipolar Smooth Windowing}: Smooth contour shape transitions between transient-preserving percussion/FX mode and seamless sustain/swell mode.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Dual Bandpass Crossover}: Draggable low-cut and high-cut frequency filters with dedicated Band Solo auditioning.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Upper-Octave Shimmer & Reverse}: Layer an octave-up granular sheen or flip slice playback direction.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Tempo-Synced Fade In/Out}: Cleanly eliminates edge transients or creates musical fade swells.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Interactive Modern UI}: Live waveform visualizer with position playhead indicator and scalable HiDPI text zoom (100% - 140%).\sa180\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 8. Creative / VintageFlux\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Path}: {\f1 Creative/VintageFlux.jsfx}\line {\b Description}: 6-Module Vintage Multi-FX & Lo-Fi Color Workstation\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\cf1 [image: screenshots/vintageflux.webp]\cf0}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Key Features}:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b 6 Dedicated Vintage FX Modules}:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li1080 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Noise}: Vinyl, Cassette, VHS, and White noise with envelope following and ducking.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li1080 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Wobble}: Pitch wow & flutter with rate and stereo drift.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li1080 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Distort}: Tube, Tape, Crunch, and Wavefold saturation with focused frequency crossover.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li1080 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Digital}: Sample rate downsampling and bitcrushing with smoothing and pass/cut modes.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li1080 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Space}: Ambient algorithmic reverb with pre-delay, decay, and damping controls.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li1080 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Magnetic}: Vintage tape wear, dropouts, and flutter imperfections.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Global Magnitude Slider}: Scales all module intensities and master character simultaneously.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Dedicated Flux Controls}: Organic, non-repeating random analog drift on every module.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Master Tone & Filters}: 12/24 dB Low/High cuts, Tilt/Smile tone EQ, M/S width, and output trim.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Scalable UI}: HiDPI text zoom presets (100% - 140%).\sa180\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 9. Delay / EchoForge\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Path}: {\f1 Delay/EchoForge.jsfx}\line {\b Description}: Analog Tape, Lo-Fi & Diffused Delay Workstation\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\cf1 [image: screenshots/echoforge.webp]\cf0}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Key Features}:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b 4 Delay Models}: Mono, Stereo, Ping-Pong, and Off (standalone Lo-Fi / Modulation / Reverb FX processor).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Tempo Sync & Free Milliseconds}: Tempo-quantized 16th steps (1 to 16) or free-running delay times from 1 ms to 1000 ms.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Tape Pitch Glide vs Keep Pitch}: Switch between classic tape-style Doppler pitch slewing or clickless crossfaded time changes.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Self-Oscillation & Analog Distortion}: Feedback up to 150% with tape-modeled saturation and soft limiter protection.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Resonant Multi-Mode Filter}: Low-Pass, High-Pass, and Band-Pass filter in the feedback path with adjustable resonance.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b 4-Stage Stereo All-Pass Diffuser}: Smears delay repeats into expansive, lush ambient reverb washes.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Lo-Fi Degradation Engine}: Continuous sample rate downsampling (down to 1 kHz) and bitcrushing (down to 2 bits).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Multi-Destination Modulation}: Dedicated LFO modulating delay time and filter cutoff for tape wow & flutter or sweeping filter dub effects.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Tone Tilt, Spread & Mix}: Output tone shaping, stereo width spread, and independent dry/wet controls.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Interactive UI}: Live animated waveform and echo tap visualizer with scalable HiDPI text zoom (100% - 140%).\sa180\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 10. EQ / ConsoleQ\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Path}: {\f1 EQ/ConsoleQ.jsfx}\line {\b Description}: Hybrid Console EQ, Air Strip & FFT Spectrum Analyzer\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\cf1 [image: screenshots/consoleq.webp]\cf0}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Key Features}:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b 4-Band Console EQ}: Low, Low-Mid, High-Mid, and High frequency bands with switchable Bell and Shelf curves for LF/HF.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Console Cut Filters}: 18 dB/oct resonant High-Pass (20 - 500 Hz) and 12 dB/oct Low-Pass (3k - 22 kHz) filters.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b High-Headroom Air Band & Sub Weight}: Dedicated Air Band shelf with selectable frequencies (2.5k, 5k, 10k, 20k, 40 kHz) up to +20 dB boost, plus a Sub 10Hz resonance weight bell.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Dual Console Topologies}: Switchable E-Series (Constant Q) and G-Series (Proportional Q) response curves.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Analog Character Coloring}: Clean, Subtle, and Warm analog harmonic drive modes.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Interactive Graph Nodes}: Drag band frequency and gain handles directly on the live EQ response curve.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Real-time 2048-Point FFT Analyzer}: High-resolution spectrum visualizer switchable between Post-EQ, Pre-EQ, and Off.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Momentary Band Solo}: Hold the [S] audition button on any frequency band column to isolate its processing range.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Output Section}: Mid/Side stereo width (0% - 200%), panning, auto-gain compensation, and latched peak LED.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Scalable UI}: HiDPI text zoom presets (100% - 140%).\sa180\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel2 \b \fs28 11. EQ / PocketQ\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Path}: {\f1 EQ/PocketQ.jsfx}\line {\b Description}: Compact Console & Air Channel Strip EQ\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\cf1 [image: screenshots/pocketq.webp]\cf0}\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b Key Features}:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Fixed Musical Frequency Bands}: Tuned classic frequencies: Sub (10 Hz), 40 Hz, 160 Hz, 650 Hz, and 2.5 kHz (switchable Shelf/Bell).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Air Band}: Selectable ultra-high frequencies (2.5k, 5k, 10k, 20k, 40 kHz) with up to +20 dB boost.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Console Cut Filters}: 18 dB/oct HPF (20 - 500 Hz) and 12 dB/oct LPF (3k - 22 kHz).\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b E-Series & G-Series Modes}: Switch between tight constant Q and smooth proportional Q response.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Console Drive}: Clean vs. Warm analog harmonic drive.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Auto Gain & Phase Invert}: Output level compensation and quick polarity toggle.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Ultra-Lightweight CPU Footprint}: Zero FFT overhead, designed for tracking and heavy multi-track mixing sessions.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li720 \fi-360 \endash \tx360\tab {\b Scalable UI}: HiDPI text zoom presets (100% - 140%).\sa180\sa180\par}
